<!-- ===================== DEVELOPMENT ===================== -->
<section id="development">
  <h2>Development <small>Claude Code and MCP against the live cluster</small></h2>
  <div class="grid2">
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Workflow</h3>
      <p class="muted" style="font-size:0.85rem">Claude Code edits the bind-mounted checkout, the primary recompiles on save, and MCP lets the session inspect and drive the live nodes. The diagram is on the <a href="/overview.html#arcana-dev">homelab overview</a>.</p>
      <dl class="kv">
        <dt>Start / stop</dt><dd class="mono">make dev.up · make dev.down</dd>
        <dt>Cluster view</dt><dd class="mono">make dev.cluster · make dev.logs</dd>
        <dt>REPL</dt><dd class="mono">make dev.iex (remsh to the primary)</dd>
        <dt>Checks</dt><dd class="mono">docker exec arcana-dev make check</dd>
        <dt>Worktrees</dt><dd class="mono">.worktrees/&lt;subsystem&gt;, one DB each</dd>
      </dl>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>MCP tools</h3>
      <dl class="kv">
        <dt>Tidewave</dt><dd class="mono">/tidewave/mcp: project_eval, get_docs, get_logs, get_source_location, execute_sql_query</dd>
        <dt>Read</dt><dd class="mono">arcana_status, registry_list/get, artifact, journal_read, model, logs, tasks, approvals</dd>
        <dt>Mutating</dt><dd class="mono">arcana_lifecycle, arcana_kernel_step, arcana_conformance_reset, arcana_tasks_write</dd>
        <dt>Audit</dt><dd>every mutating call lands in journal stream <span class="mono">dev_mcp:audit</span></dd>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ===================== RUNTIME ===================== -->
<section id="runtime">
  <h2>Runtime wiring <small>owned by the homelab</small></h2>
  <div class="grid2">
    <div class="card">
      <dl class="kv">
        <dt>Source</dt><dd class="mono">{{ arcana2_src_path }} (bind-mounted at /workspace)</dd>
        <dt>Containers</dt><dd class="mono">arcana-dev :4100, arcana-dev-2 :4101</dd>
        <dt>Ports</dt><dd>127.0.0.1 plus the tailnet IP, never all interfaces</dd>
        <dt>Console</dt><dd><a href="https://{{ tailscale_hostname }}:{{ arcana2_nginx_port }}">https://{{ tailscale_hostname }}:{{ arcana2_nginx_port }}</a></dd>
        <dt>Push origin</dt><dd><a href="https://{{ tailscale_hostname }}:8443">https://{{ tailscale_hostname }}:8443</a> <span class="muted">tailscale serve, trusted cert, for mobile web push (playbooks/tailscale-serve.yml)</span></dd>
        <dt>Clustering</dt><dd>libcluster Epmd over <span class="mono">ARCANA_CLUSTER_HOSTS</span>, shared cookie</dd>
        <dt>Database</dt><dd><span class="mono">arcana_dev</span> on YugabyteDB; only the primary runs migrations</dd>
        <dt>LLM</dt><dd>Anthropic API (key in a root-only env file) and the local <span class="mono">homelab</span> profile: <span class="mono">sglang-watcher:8080</span> on homelab-net, no auth. The model cold-starts in about 90 s after 5 idle minutes.</dd>
        <dt>Playbook</dt><dd class="mono">playbooks/arcana2.yml</dd>
      </dl>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Notes</h3>
      <ul style="margin:0;padding-left:1.1rem;font-size:0.85rem">
        <li>The nodes are <span class="mono">restart: unless-stopped</span>; the follower waits for the primary's health check.</li>
        <li>Per-node state (ETS, log ring buffer, memory store) is not shared; durable state is the database plus the local store root.</li>
        <li>Durable guarantees depend on YugabyteDB. It is the homelab's only SQL database, loopback-only with auth off.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

